---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const CHECKED_ON = '22 August 2026';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Is QuadERP an accounting package?',
    a: 'Not in the sense QuickBooks is. It keeps the day to day money in order, invoices, debts, expenses and a profit and loss, but it is not double entry and it does not file anything. The accounting page sets out exactly where that line sits.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I use both?',
    a: 'Plenty of businesses do. Run the shop on QuadERP, export, and let your accountant work in whatever they prefer. The export is self-serve.',
  },
  {
    q: 'When is QuickBooks the better answer?',
    a: 'When the accounting itself is the job. If you need full double entry, statutory reporting and a package your accountant already knows inside out, buy the accounting package. We would rather say that than sell you the wrong thing.',
  },
];
---

<PageLayout page="quickbooks-alternative-ghana" faqs={faqs} faqHeading="Questions people ask when comparing">
    <p>
        This comes up often enough to be worth a straight answer. QuickBooks is accounting
        software and it is good at being accounting software. The question is whether accounting
        software is what a shop with a counter, shelves and staff actually needs to buy first.
    </p>

    <h2>They solve different halves of the same business</h2>
    <p>
        An accounting package starts from transactions that have already happened. A retail
        system starts at the counter, where the transaction is created, and works outward into
        stock, staff and the money. If you only have the first, somebody has to feed it, and that
        somebody is usually you, in the evening.
    </p>

    <div class="erp-compare-wrap">
        <table class="erp-compare-table">
            <thead>
                <tr><th>What you need</th><th>QuadERP</th><th>An accounting package</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>Ring up a sale at the counter</td><td>Yes, that is the starting point</td><td>Not what it is for</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Stock levels that move when you sell</td><td>Yes</td><td>Not what it is for</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Which staff member sold what</td><td>Yes</td><td>Not what it is for</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Several branches in one view</td><td>Yes, on Multi-Branch</td><td>Varies by product and tier</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Invoices and who owes you</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Full double entry and a balance sheet</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Statutory filing</td><td>No</td><td>Yes, that is the point of it</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p class="erp-checked-on">
        The QuadERP column is checked against what ships today. The right-hand column is
        deliberately generic, because accounting products differ by tier and we are not going to
        quote someone else's feature list back at you from memory. Checked {CHECKED_ON}.
    </p>

    <h2>Where we would tell you to buy QuickBooks instead</h2>
    <p>
        If the accounting is the job, buy the accounting package. If you need a trial balance, a
        balance sheet, full double entry or statutory filing, QuadERP does not do those and is
        not pretending to. That is written out on
        <a href="/accounting-software-ghana/">the accounting page</a> in more detail than most
        vendors would put on their own site.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do that an accounts package does not</h2>
    <p>
        The shop floor. Selling on a phone or a laptop with no terminal to buy, Mobile Money as a
        first-class payment method, stock that moves as you sell, reorder alerts, transfers
        between branches, and a record of which staff member did what. Prices in cedis, and we
        set it up and train your staff rather than emailing you a login.
    </p>
    <p>
        The detail is on <a href="/pos-system-ghana/">the POS page</a> and
        <a href="/inventory-management-software/">the inventory page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Using both</h2>
    <p>
        This is the common ending. Run the shop on QuadERP, export whenever your accountant asks,
        and let them work in the tool they already know. The export is a button you press
        yourself, not a request you send us.
    </p>
</PageLayout>
